      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"3\">Level 3 - Intermediate</span>\n    <span class=\"time\">25 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Structural pattern</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Tier 3</span>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Flyweight</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">When you need a hundred thousand tiny objects that are mostly the same, store the shared part once and pass the varying part in from outside. Learn intrinsic vs extrinsic state, the flyweight factory, why <code>Integer 127 == 127</code> is true but <code>128 == 128</code> is false, and how the kernel's shared zero page is the same trick.</p>\n"
  },
